    "youtubeId": "kYJjZfW8uVo",
    "keyNotes": "• Birth and Early Life of Jesus:\n  - Born in Bethlehem of Judea to the Virgin Mary under the Roman reign of Caesar Augustus.\n  - Raised in Nazareth of Galilee where he grew in wisdom, stature, and favor with God and humans (Luke 2:52). Worked as a carpenter.\n• Baptism of Jesus:\n  - Baptized by John the Baptist in the River Jordan at age thirty.\n  - Significance: To fulfill all righteousness, identify with sinful humanity, and launch his public ministry. The Holy Spirit descended like a dove, and the Father's voice declared: 'This is my beloved Son, in whom I am well pleased.'\n• The Temptations in the Wilderness:\n  - Led by the Spirit into the Judean wilderness; fasted 40 days and nights and was tempted by Satan on three fronts:\n    1. Turn stones to bread (Temptation of physical appetite): Jesus answered: 'Man shall not live by bread alone, but by every word that proceeds from the mouth of God.'\n    2. Jump from the pinnacle of the Temple (Temptation of sensational pride): Jesus replied: 'You shall not tempt the Lord your God.'\n    3. Bow and worship Satan for all kingdoms of the world (Temptation of political compromise and idolatry): Jesus commanded: 'Away with you, Satan! For it is written, You shall worship the Lord your God, and Him only you shall serve.'\n• Selection of the Twelve Disciples:\n  - Chose ordinary men (fishermen like Peter, James, John, Andrew; a despised tax collector like Matthew) after spending an entire night in prayer.\n• Core Teachings and Ethical Pillars:\n  - The Sermon on the Mount (The Beatitudes - Matthew 5): Blessed are the poor in spirit, the meek, the peacemakers, the pure in heart.\n  - Love for Enemies: 'Love your enemies, bless those who curse you, do good to those who hate you.'\n  - The Golden Rule: 'Whatever you want men to do to you, do also to them.'\n  - Forgiveness: Forgiving others seventy times seven (unlimited forgiveness).\n  - Compassion for the Vulnerable: Reaching out to lepers, outcasts, prostitutes, and widows.",
